{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794156958,"nonce":"wTXf98RA7VXdYu1WwKKY626P74s=","message":"## As built, two more departures\n\nTwo more points of 514eb0d0 differ from the design above, besides the two already noted.\n\n3. **The editor is run through `sh`, with the file as its one argument** (`sh -c '\u003ceditor\u003e \"$1\"' sh \u003cfile\u003e`). The editor git names is a shell command, as git's is, so one with arguments of its own (`code --wait`) runs, and the shell, not git-work, quotes the path, so a path with a space in it is one argument.\n4. **Trailing whitespace is trimmed from what comes back.** An editor ends a file with a newline nobody typed; trimmed, an editor that only adds it leaves the draft as it was, and the box gets no blank line at its end. The indent of the first line is kept.\n\nPoint (2) of the earlier as-built comment, the one-key flag after a slow `esc`, does not hold any more: 8fcaf781 (1ff9ab2f) made `esc` in a text open the palette over it, and the flag was removed.","files":null}]}